From 9052d53dc95dabc4ba21fb8f9d1cd254a8478a5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 00:47:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] CCDYHOME9050: on HT9050 CCD Y (M108) 'at home' = homed + near
 0, the home lamp is not asked -- EastSun 1008 'CCD Y home check stops my
 Index Z' -> 'split with the HT9050 flag; homed + position near 0'.

00:31 MCCDY homed at 0 but its home lamp went off at the switch edge (DS402 home); 910 MoveIndexZ's interlock (exactly 0 AND lamp on) refused every Index Z descent (00:31:28 message). atester_FinePitch.cpp MoveIndexZ (910 mymotor :6631) and acarry.cpp W906_ShtCcdYHome (Out Shuttle 1 / 2 moves): HT9050 (9050GPIB or Type_HT9050) = HomeFlag 1 and |pos| <= 100; other machines: 910. Same lines.
tests: test_fp9050_index.cpp -- fidelity edit list + 910 :6631; [F5] + 'homed at 0, lamp off: descent commanded'; Q4b refusal at 500 (was 5). test_ht9050_shtsafe.cpp -- M108 HomeFlag follows g_ccdHome, + 'homed at -100, lamp off: may move'. FP9050_Pure, FP9050_Index, HT9050_ShtSafe, Flow9050_Shuttle, HT9050_DryRun passed. Release linked; Debug compiled (link waits for EastSun's program). WORKLOG row 196.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
